# 11. Python function arguments

The custom Python language supports:

### Positional arguments

```python
foo(a, b, c)
```

### Keyword arguments

```python
render_template(
    "index.jinja",
    title=title,
    products=products
)
```

The grammar has:

```text
argument
    : expr
    | IDENTIFIER ASSIGN expr
```



The AST has:

```text
PositionalArgument
KeywordArgument
```



---

# 12. Python indentation / blocks

Your custom Python lexer has explicit support for:

```text
NEWLINE
INDENT
DEDENT
```

and tracks indentation levels itself.

It also handles indentation changes and emits synthetic `INDENT`/`DEDENT` tokens.

So these are supported:

```python
if x:
    a = 1
    b = 2
```

and nested blocks:

```python
if x:
    for p in products:
        if p.price > 100:
            ...
```

---

# 13. Python comments

The lexer supports:

```python
# this is a comment
```

using:

```text
COMMENT : '#' ~[\r\n]* -> skip
```



---

# 14. Python operator precedence

The Python grammar has the expression hierarchy:

```text
OR
→ AND
→ NOT
→ comparison
→ + -
→ * / %
→ unary -
→ atom
```

So the grammar does distinguish operator levels.

